    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/events-officer-crawley-wa-australia-82440f31-6163-4f9d-8bd4-a3d9a5dbf055": {
      "title": "Events Officer",
      "description": "Events Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Events Officer 524590 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Join a collaborative team that helps showcase the best of UWA and strengthens connections with students and the wider community. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Brand Marketing and Recruitment (BMR) division is responsible for showcasing the best of The University of Western Australia, strengthening the University's reputation and supporting student engagement and growth. Bringing together marketing, communications, engagement and events expertise, BMR delivers integrated strategies that connect UWA with future students, alumni, partners and the broader community. Within BMR, the Brand and Engagement team serves as a strategic and creative hub, building meaningful connections through brand campaigns, partnerships, content, school engagement and major institutional events. The team ensures that every interaction with UWA reflects a consistent, authentic and engaging brand experience. About the opportunity As an Events Officer, you will work with stakeholders across the University to design and deliver meaningful experiences that advance UWA's strategic objectives and strengthen engagement with key audiences. Working across a diverse portfolio of events, you will act as a trusted advisor, helping stakeholders shape ideas, identify opportunities and translate objectives into impactful event experiences. From executive functions and graduation ceremonies to community engagement and strategic institutional events, you will provide expert guidance while leading the planning and delivery process from concept through to evaluation. Success in this role requires strong project management capability, sound judgement and the ability to coordinate multiple workstreams simultaneously. You will bring together specialist teams, suppliers and stakeholders to deliver high-quality outcomes, ensuring projects remain on track, within budget and aligned with University priorities, governance requirements and brand standards. About you Experience managing complex projects or events involving multiple stakeholders, workstreams and deadlines. Strong consultation and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to advise, influence and build trusted relationships. Highly developed planning and organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities. Relevant tertiary qualification or demonstrated equivalent competency. Demonstrated ability to work independently, show initiative and work as part of a team. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. The role also requires flexibility to work outside standard business hours, including occasional weekends, and the ability to undertake event-related physical tasks. Some interstate or overseas travel may be required. Position description: PD - Events Officer (524590).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Katie Fendick at katie.fendick@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 25 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 20d9b80c Last Name (required) 46b1060b Email (required) 15aea252 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Senior Technician (Safety) Crawley, WA Technical/Laboratory support Be a key driver of safety culture and compliance across diverse research and teaching environments. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a91e36dd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Community Engagement/Marketing Community Engagement/Marketing Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 3456d567 Last Name (required) 6def8b1b Email (required) 3b71db3e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
