    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/investment-analyst-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Investment Analyst",
      "description": "Investment Analyst - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Investment Analyst 524563 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 21 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Investment Analyst (524563) Shape strategic decisions through high-quality analysis of UWA’s debt, investment and endowment portfolios. Join a specialist Treasury & Investments team with broad exposure to portfolio risk, funding strategy and executive reporting. Full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Finance supports the responsible stewardship of the University’s finances through strategic financial and commercial advice, governance frameworks, procurement, financial operations, and management of UWA’s investment and endowment portfolios. The Treasury & Investments team provides portfolio oversight, analysis and advice that supports sound decisions across the University. About the opportunity Monitor the performance, risk, cash flows, valuations and policy compliance of UWA’s debt and investment portfolios, and provide clear portfolio reporting, market commentary and recommendations to senior leaders and committees. Deliver fundamental and quantitative analysis across credit, interest rate, liquidity and counterparty risk; build financial models and scenario analysis; and identify risks and opportunities arising from market, economic, regulatory and geopolitical developments. Support funding, refinancing and liability management initiatives while strengthening investment and treasury policies, dashboards, reporting automation, governance processes and audit-ready documentation. About you A relevant tertiary qualification in finance, economics, accounting, mathematics or a related discipline, combined with extensive relevant experience. Extensive experience in investment reporting, portfolio analytics or treasury operations, with strong financial modelling and advanced Excel capability. Sound knowledge of fixed income markets, credit analysis, interest rate concepts, liquidity and treasury practices. Strong analytical judgement, attention to detail and the ability to interpret complex financial information and translate it into clear insights and recommendations. Well-developed written, verbal and stakeholder communication skills, with the ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance and finance check will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Investment Analyst PD.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Jason Chesters at Jason.Chesters@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zander Ribbens at Zander.Ribbens@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday 21st October This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 62f12fe3 Last Name (required) b8e8cc55 Email (required) d0e55ef9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a67e7ed7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance Finance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 073fa04c Last Name (required) 2c6ab722 Email (required) dcf39873 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
