    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-indigenous-postgraduate-student-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Indigenous Postgraduate Student Officer",
      "description": "Senior Indigenous Postgraduate Student Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Indigenous Postgraduate Student Officer 524642 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 20 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Play a pivotal role in empowering Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander postgraduate and Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students to thrive and succeed at UWA. Lead impactful student recruitment, outreach, engagement and retention initiatives that strengthen Indigenous postgraduate pathways and future leadership. Identified position: This role is open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander applicants only, in accordance with Section 50(d) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA). Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis. Base salary range: Level 7, $108,413 – $120,287 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor Indigenous (DVCI) provides leadership across UWA’s Indigenous Portfolio and drives the development and implementation of Indigenous strategy across the University. The Portfolio provides strategic leadership for the School of Indigenous Studies and Indigenous student support services, while advancing opportunities for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples through education, research and employment initiatives. Working within the Indigenous Student Centre, you will join a dedicated team committed to enhancing access, participation, retention and success for Indigenous students across their educational journey. The Portfolio plays a significant role in developing future Indigenous leaders, supporting Indigenous knowledges, and delivering culturally responsive programs and services across UWA. About the opportunity Lead and coordinate outreach, recruitment and engagement initiatives that attract Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students into postgraduate and Higher Degree by Research (HDR) study pathways. Design and deliver student success, retention and progression programs, providing culturally responsive guidance, advocacy and holistic support throughout the postgraduate student journey. Partner with students, academic staff and professional teams to enhance the Indigenous postgraduate student experience, while contributing to strategic initiatives, operational improvements and continuous service enhancement. About you Degree qualification and substantial relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training and demonstrated expertise in student services, Indigenous education or a related field. Strong knowledge of the Western Australian education sector, Indigenous higher education, and Higher Degree by Research (HDR) administration, policies and processes. Demonstrated experience delivering exceptional student support, student engagement and customer service outcomes, particularly for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students. Highly developed communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships, provide advocacy and communicate effectively and sensitively with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities. Proven ability to coordinate programs, manage competing priorities, lead operational activities and implement service improvements using sound judgement and initiative. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current WA Working with Children Check, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. This position is only available for Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Island people as permitted under Section 50(d) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 . UWA believes that an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander individual would bring essential insights and understanding to this role, enhancing the university’s ability to connect with and serve the community effectively. Position description: Senior Indigenous Postgraduate Student Officer - 524642.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Sabrina Swift at sabrina.swift@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. Please ensure you upload a copy of your most recent Resume and a document demonstrating how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 20 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Queries regarding indigenous aspects of the role may be directed to indigenous.workforce@uwa.edu.au To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) bf9b6285 Last Name (required) 74c71f4b Email (required) 522c7289 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9de345e9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Administration / Support Services Student Administration / Support Services Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) f3ce6548 Last Name (required) 80ba4ee6 Email (required) 44960249 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/indigenous-student-success-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Indigenous Student Success Officer",
      "description": "Indigenous Student Success Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Indigenous Student Success Officer 524631 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 20 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Make a meaningful difference by supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students to thrive throughout their university journey. Join a dedicated team committed to Indigenous student success, engagement, belonging and educational achievement at one of Australia's leading universities. Identified position: This role is open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander applicants only, in accordance with Section 50(d) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA). Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis. Base salary range: Level 6, $99,040.00 – $104,669.00 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor Indigenous (DVCI) provides leadership across UWA's Indigenous Portfolio, driving initiatives that support Indigenous student success, Indigenous workforce development, teaching, research and community engagement. Working in partnership across the University, the Indigenous Portfolio is committed to empowering Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, fostering future leaders, and advancing Indigenous knowledges. The Indigenous Students Centre plays a vital role in supporting current Indigenous students through culturally safe services, programs and opportunities that enhance academic achievement, wellbeing, engagement and a strong sense of belonging throughout the student lifecycle. About the opportunity Provide culturally appropriate support, advice, pastoral care and academic assistance to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, helping them navigate university life and achieve their educational goals. Coordinate and deliver student engagement programs, events, scholarship support, tutoring initiatives and activities that strengthen student success, retention, wellbeing and belonging. Build strong relationships with students, community organisations and internal stakeholders while contributing to outreach, work-integrated learning opportunities, reporting, administration and continuous service improvement. About you Demonstrated experience supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, with a strong understanding of Indigenous student success, engagement and higher education pathways. Proven ability to work respectfully and effectively with Aboriginal peoples, communities and organisations, supported by a strong understanding of Indigenous cultures and perspectives. Highly developed communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage a diverse range of stakeholders and provide professional, student-centred support. Excellent organisational and administrative skills, with demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, coordinate programs and meet deadlines. Relevant degree qualification and subsequent experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, training and specialist expertise. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current WA Working with Children Check, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. This position is only available for Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Island people as permitted under Section 50(d) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 . UWA believes that an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander individual would bring essential insights and understanding to this role, enhancing the university’s ability to connect with and serve the community effectively. Position description: Indigenous Student Success Officer - 524631.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Sabrina Swift at sabrina.swift@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. Please ensure you upload a copy of your current resume and a document outlining how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 20 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Queries regarding indigenous aspects of the role may be directed to indigenous.workforce@uwa.edu.au To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 80f0538d Last Name (required) ebc1872e Email (required) d2598115 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 060d1bf9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Administration / Support Services Student Administration / Support Services Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) f7323049 Last Name (required) 8eef345e Email (required) 0e64e37e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
