    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/indigenous-future-student-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Indigenous Future Student Officer",
      "description": "Indigenous Future Student Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Indigenous Future Student Officer 524632 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 20 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Make a meaningful impact by supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students on their journey to higher education. Build strong connections with schools, communities and future students across Western Australia through outreach and engagement programs. Identified position: This role is open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander applicants only, in accordance with Section 50(d) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA). Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis. Base salary range: Level 6, $99,040.00 – $104,669.00 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor Indigenous (DVCI) provides strategic leadership for Indigenous initiatives across The University of Western Australia. Through education, student support, research and community engagement, the Indigenous Portfolio works to advance opportunities for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, strengthen Indigenous participation in higher education, and support the development of future leaders. The Indigenous Students Centre plays a vital role in creating pathways to university and supporting Indigenous students throughout their educational journey. Working closely with schools, communities and internal stakeholders, the team delivers programs and initiatives that encourage participation, improve access and create positive student outcomes. About the opportunity Coordinate and deliver outreach, engagement and recruitment activities for prospective Indigenous students, including school visits, regional travel, community engagement and presentations. Build and maintain strong relationships with schools, community organisations, prospective students and key university stakeholders to support Indigenous participation in higher education. Provide high-quality advice, administrative support and student pathway information, including guidance on scholarships, accommodation, ABSTUDY and university entry options. About you Demonstrated experience supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, communities or educational initiatives. Proven ability to engage effectively with Aboriginal peoples, community organisations and external stakeholders, building trusted and productive relationships. Knowledge of the Western Australian education system and Indigenous higher education pathways, combined with the ability to deliver workshops, presentations and outreach activities. Highly developed written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, with a strong customer service and community engagement focus. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, supported by strong organisational, administrative and digital literacy skills. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current WA Working with Children Check, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. This position is only available for Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Island people as permitted under Section 50(d) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 . UWA believes that an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander individual would bring essential insights and understanding to this role, enhancing the university’s ability to connect with and serve the community effectively. Position description: Indigenous Future Students Officer - 524632.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Sabrina Swift at sabrina.swift@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. Please ensure you upload a copy of your current resume and a document outlining how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 20 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Queries regarding indigenous aspects of the role may be directed to indigenous.workforce@uwa.edu.au To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 41b7f1d5 Last Name (required) b62b23c4 Email (required) 1d9b3e13 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert eacb9f73 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Administration / Support Services Student Administration / Support Services Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 7b93232e Last Name (required) 48372deb Email (required) 92bb7995 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We 