    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/research-and-administrative-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Research and Administrative Officer",
      "description": "Research and Administrative Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Research and Administrative Officer 524613 Crawley, WA Part Time Closing on: 27 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Flexible working hours. Part-time (0.8 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 3 years. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The School of Agriculture and Environment at The University of Western Australia is located within one of the world's recognised biodiversity hotspots and is home to internationally leading research in agricultural and environmental sciences. The School is ranked 1st in Australia and 13th globally for Agricultural Sciences, and is recognised for excellence in soil science, environmental science and engineering. Working within the Institute of Agriculture, you will support the research group led by Professor Brajesh Singh, contributing to a vibrant, multidisciplinary environment that collaborates with researchers, industry partners, policymakers and international stakeholders to address some of the most significant challenges facing sustainable agriculture and environmental management. About the opportunity Provide high-level administrative support, including coordination of travel, purchasing, editorial activities and day-to-day research operations. Lead promotion and engagement activities across social media platforms, industry events and stakeholder networks to enhance the visibility of research programs and the Journal of Sustainable Agriculture & Environment. Support research projects through laboratory and field administration, including coordinating consumables, maintaining records, assisting with glasshouse and field experiments, and liaising with researchers, journal teams and external partners. About you Degree qualification in agriculture, environmental science, biological sciences or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education. Demonstrated experience in administration, coordination or project support roles, with strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build productive relationships with researchers, industry partners, stakeholders and multidisciplinary teams. Experience creating and coordinating content across social media and digital engagement platforms such as LinkedIn, YouTube, X (Twitter), Instagram and TikTok. Strong digital literacy, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, databases, online systems and the ability to work independently, use initiative and solve problems effectively. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current “C” class driver’s licence is preferred. Position description: Position Description - Research and Administrative Officer (524613).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Professor Brajesh Singh at brajesh.singh@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Maddy Chaplin at maddy.chaplin@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 27 October 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fe3eb8a5 Last Name (required) 27274103 Email (required) 2ac5b211 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 704cfa60 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration & Executive support Administration & Executive support Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) f8019a63 Last Name (required) 9603950f Email (required) aa386c57 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. 