    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-genomics-qeii-medical-centre-scgh-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer - Genomics  - QEII Medical Centre / SCGH, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Lecturer - Genomics 524540 QEII Medical Centre / SCGH, WA Full Time Closing on: 3 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Shape the future of human genomics and precision health through impactful teaching, research and industry engagement. Establish and lead a nationally recognised research program in a rapidly growing discipline with strong opportunities for collaboration across health, medical and scientific fields. Full – Time  (1.0 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis Base salary range: Level C, $149,909 – $172.441 p.a.  plus 17% superannuation. About the area The School of Biomedical Sciences at The University of Western Australia (UWA) is a leading centre for education and research across biological, medical and health sciences. Located within the renowned QEII Medical Campus, the School is embedded in one of Australia's most dynamic biomedical precincts, alongside major teaching hospitals, research institutes and clinical partners. Within the School, the Discipline of Medical Science and Genetics delivers innovative undergraduate and postgraduate education in human genomics, medical science and related biomedical disciplines. The Discipline plays a key role in UWA's Human Genomics major and contributes to a range of health, medicine and bioinformatics programs. Researchers benefit from modern laboratory facilities, strong interdisciplinary partnerships and a collaborative environment that supports translational and discovery-based research. About the opportunity Lead and grow an externally funded research program in human genomics, precision health, genomic medicine, bioinformatics or a closely related field, producing high-impact research outcomes and supervising Honours, Masters and PhD students. Develop, coordinate and deliver innovative undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, including curriculum development, assessment design and student supervision across human genomics and related biomedical sciences programs. Build strategic collaborations with researchers, clinicians, industry partners, government agencies and community stakeholders to advance research, education and real-world impact. About you PhD in human genomics, precision health, bioinformatics, computational biology or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated track record of research excellence, including high-quality peer-reviewed publications, success in securing competitive research funding and experience supervising higher degree research students. Expertise in contemporary genomic technologies, genomic data analysis, genomic medicine and/or precision health, with the ability to establish a recognised research profile. Experience delivering high-quality tertiary teaching, curriculum development, innovative learning design and student-centred assessment practices. Strong stakeholder engagement, collaboration and communication skills, with a demonstrated commitment to inclusion, diversity, equity, consumer engagement and community impact Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A WA Working with Children Check will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Senior Lecturer, Genomics (524540).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Charlene Kahler, Head of School at charlene.kahler@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at pratik.sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in the attached position description document.  Please attach your response  in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday 3 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 750ac843 Last Name (required) d097b8fd Email (required) c630903f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a43f0073 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations QEII Medical Centre / SCGH, WA, Australia QEII Medical Centre / SCGH, WA, Australia First Name (required) 3065637a Last Name (required) c2e09fad Email (required) ada392ab Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its function