    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/facility-supervisor-unihall-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Facility Supervisor, UniHall",
      "description": "Facility Supervisor, UniHall - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Facility Supervisor, UniHall 524628 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 19 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Deliver exceptional residential living experience for students and guests at UWA's UniHall. Coordinate maintenance across a diverse accommodation and facilities portfolio. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Campus Management is responsible for the planning, development, management and operation of UWA's physical estate and infrastructure. Through integrated property, facilities, asset management and maintenance services, the team supports safe, sustainable and high-performing environments for learning, research and campus life. This role is embedded within UWA's residential communities of UniHall. Working closely with residents, staff, contractors and service providers, you will help ensure that accommodation facilities are safe, well maintained and enhance the overall resident and guest experience. About the opportunity Coordinate reactive and preventative maintenance programs across UniHall facilities, ensuring compliance, service quality and asset performance. Act as the key liaison between residents, contractors, service providers and Campus Management, driving high-quality facilities management and customer service outcomes and an exceptional residential living experience. Monitor building condition, contractor performance, cleaning services and asset maintenance activities, providing advice on repairs and minor works while identifying opportunities upgrades and continuous improvement. About you Qualification in a relevant trade discipline or equivalent experience and competency in property management or operations, along with a current, valid WA Working with Children card. Substantial experience in coordinating building maintenance and services, with demonstrated organisational skills and the ability to prioritise competing demands. Ability to support preventive maintenance as a strategy in maintaining University facilities and equipment, including but not limited to mechanical, electrical, plumbing, fire protection, and associated control systems. Highly developed communication skills and the ability to interact in a positive manner with the campus community and stakeholders to achieve outcomes. Ability to read and interpret Australian Standards, BCA, federal, state and local codes. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance, WA Working with Children Check, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. Some after-hours work may be required. Position description: PD - Facility Supervisor, UniHall (524628).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Melita O’Donnell at melita.odonnell@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume (max. 4 pages) and Cover Letter (max. 2 pages) should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday, 19 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 05a80571 Last Name (required) 58b9f6c1 Email (required) 741f5d97 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 38d10b5c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Campus / facilities management Campus / facilities management Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 943c109a Last Name (required) 826860d6 Email (required) c8cb4ba8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/facility-supervisor-crawley-village-and-forrest-hall-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Facility Supervisor, Crawley Village and Forrest Hall",
      "description": "Facility Supervisor, Crawley Village and Forrest Hall - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Facility Supervisor, Crawley Village and Forrest Hall 524627 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 19 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Deliver exceptional resident and guest experiences across UWA accommodation. Lead maintenance, asset management and service delivery outcomes. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Campus Management is responsible for the planning, development, management and operation of UWA’s physical estate and infrastructure. Through integrated property, facilities, asset management, capital works and operational services, the team provides safe, sustainable and efficient environments that support teaching, research and community engagement. Within Infrastructure Maintenance, this role is dedicated to supporting the residential communities of Crawley Village and Forrest Hall. Working closely with residents, stakeholders, contractors and service providers, you will help ensure facilities are well-maintained, compliant, welcoming and fit for purpose. About the opportunity Coordinate reactive and planned preventative maintenance programs across residential facilities, ensuring compliance, safety, asset reliability and service excellence. Act as the primary facilities liaison for residents and stakeholders, managing maintenance priorities, contractor performance, cleaning services and estate-related operations while ensuring high-quality service delivery and exception resident experience. Conduct inspections, audits and asset management activities while providing expert advice on maintenance, repairs and minor works, monitoring estate-related issues and identifying opportunities for continuous improvement and. About you Qualifications in a relevant trade discipline or equivalent experience and competency, along with a current, valid WA Working with Children card. Substantial experience in coordinating building maintenance and services, with demonstrated organisations skills and the ability to prioritise competing demands. Ability to support preventive maintenance as a strategy in maintaining University facilities and equipment, including but not limited to mechanical, electrical, plumbing, fire protection, and associated control systems. Highly developed communication skills and the ability to interact in a positive manner with the campus community and stakeholders to achieve outcomes. Ability to read and interpret Australian Standards, BCA, federal, state and local codes, and apply sound judgement to maintenance and compliance-related issues. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance, WA Working with Children Check, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. Some after-hours work may be required. Position description: PD - Facility Supervisor, Crawley Village and Forrest Hall (524627).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Melita O’Donnell at melita.odonnell@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume (max. 4 pages) and Cover Letter (max. 2 pages) should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday, 19 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 04ff4162 Last Name (required) 9d3dd8cd Email (required) 35947825 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 030a3fc5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Campus / facilities management Campus / facilities management Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) d88d5319 Last Name (required) 2f197035 Email (required) 17c17739 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will resp