    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/mental-health-and-wellbeing-practitioner-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Mental Health and Wellbeing Practitioner",
      "description": "Mental Health and Wellbeing Practitioner - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Mental Health and Wellbeing Practitioner 524528 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 19 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Make a meaningful impact on student mental health, safety and academic success through prevention, early intervention and responsive support. Join a collaborative wellbeing team delivering evidence-informed counselling, education and capacity-building initiatives. Full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Student Life and Community supports UWA’s commitment to delivering a world-class, inclusive and student-centred experience. Working across the student lifecycle, the Directorate provides integrated services and initiatives that promote participation, belonging, safety, health, wellbeing, accessibility and positive engagement with university life. Within this Directorate, Student Health and Wellbeing delivers an integrated continuum of prevention, early intervention, therapeutic support and recovery services. The team leads mental health and wellbeing initiatives, low-barrier student support, primary prevention education, and trauma-informed responses for students affected by gender-based violence and other harmful behaviours. About the opportunity Deliver evidence-informed prevention activities, wellbeing education and training, together with brief, solution-focused counselling and specialist support for students experiencing mental health, psychosocial or safety concerns. Conduct risk assessments, develop collaborative safety plans, and facilitate coordinated case management and referrals across University and external services. Build the capability of staff and student communities through specialist advice, training and wellbeing initiatives, while contributing to clinical supervision, service evaluation, record keeping and continuous improvement. About you A relevant degree with subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training and professional experience. Current registration or membership with a relevant professional body, such as the Australian Association of Social Workers, Psychotherapy and Counselling Federation of Australia, or Australian Counselling Association. Demonstrated experience delivering evidence-based brief therapeutic interventions and solution-focused counselling for people experiencing mental health, wellbeing or psychosocial concerns. Experience responding to disclosures of harm and gender-based violence, including family and domestic violence, together with demonstrated capability in crisis intervention, suicide risk assessment and safety planning. Strong communication, consultation and organisational skills, with experience delivering community education, training or wellbeing programs and the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance, and WA Working with Children Check, will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Mental Health & Wellbeing Practitioner PD.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Linda Jenkins at Linda.Jenkins@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zander Ribbens at Zander.Ribbens@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday 19th October This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 0a9416d7 Last Name (required) 5f53bb04 Email (required) 0691daf5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2b5badfa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Administration / Support Services Student Administration / Support Services Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) d83aafd6 Last Name (required) 4f6a53c9 Email (required) 1402abb2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services