    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-management-accountant-infrastructure-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Management Accountant (Infrastructure)",
      "description": "Senior Management Accountant (Infrastructure) - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Management Accountant (Infrastructure) 524587 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 18 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Shape the financial future of major infrastructure and capital investments at one of Australia's leading universities. Partner with senior leaders to drive operational efficiency, optimise capital investment and deliver strategic financial insights that support informed decision-making and long-term financial sustainability. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The role of Finance is to support the appropriate stewardship of the University’s finance through the provision of a strategic financial and commercial advice, establishment of a financial management framework, financial management tools, procurement, management of the University’s Investment and Endowment portfolio, as well as financial oversight and accountability for finance administrative and transactional operations. Finance undertakes this role through four core pillars: Financial Compliance, Financial Performance, Treasury & Investment and Procurement. In undertaking this role, Finance operates support across the University, from advising the Vice-Chancellery, Executive and Senior leadership team on strategy and performance to supporting staff and students in their purchases and travel arrangements. About the opportunity Lead financial planning, budgeting, forecasting and reporting activities for the University's infrastructure and capital portfolio, providing trusted advice to senior stakeholders and project leaders. Deliver advanced financial modelling, business case analysis, capital investment planning and risk mitigation strategies that support informed decision-making and long-term financial sustainability. Drive continuous improvement initiatives across financial reporting, performance management and capital project governance while building strong partnerships across the University community. About you Relevant tertiary qualification or demonstrated equivalent competency in Capital/Infrastructure Accounting. Full professional membership of a recognised Australian, or International accounting body. Substantial and extensive experience in financial capital and infrastructure planning for large organisations with multiple funding arrangements. Demonstrated experience and expertise in coordinating, preparing and monitoring complex consolidated budgets, forecasting and income/expenditure management. Demonstrated experience in financial modelling. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Senior Management Accountant (Infrastructure) (524587).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Joyce Odchigue at joyce.odchigue@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 18 October 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 74580774 Last Name (required) 06032c66 Email (required) cdb19535 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Brand Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Coordinate and deliver integrated brand campaigns and initiatives across multiple channels, at WA’s top university. Academic Services Officer Port Hedland, WA Administration & Executive support Based in Port Hedland I Play a key role in supporting medical students undertaking rural clinical training across Western Australia. Events Officer Crawley, WA Community Engagement/Marketing Deliver high-quality events and experiences that strengthen engagement, support strategic priorities and showcase the best of UWA to internal and external audiences. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 075425a1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance Finance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) a3ccbbcb Last Name (required) 6746ac81 Email (required) 7bc345fb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
